From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ep9
Subject: [PATCH] Add Regex::match_at_limited: one match attempt at one
 position

JavaScript's sticky flag (y) asks for a match that starts exactly at
lastIndex. With only find_from_* an embedder must search from lastIndex
and drop a match that starts later, so a failing sticky exec scans the
whole rest of the text: a lexer built from sticky regexes becomes
quadratic.

match_at_limited tries the pattern at one code unit position and
returns that match or None, with the same Limits as find_limited.

Test: tests/match_at.rs (a failed attempt on a 100,000 unit text takes
a few steps).
---
